JD 4:

Requirements

Key ResponsibilitiesA. Buying, Sourcing & Supplier Management
Own end-to-end buying for General Merchandise categories, including identifying, evaluating, and onboarding new manufacturers and suppliers.
Develop strong vendor relationships and lead negotiations on pricing, margins, trade terms, and payment conditions.
Continuously expand and optimize the supplier base to enhance cost efficiency, quality, and assortment breadth.
Conduct regular vendor performance reviews covering supply reliability, quality, and commercial outcomes.

B. Assortment Building & Pricing
Curate region-specific and seasonally relevant assortments aligned with customer needs and value perception.
Benchmark pricing across offline and online channels to maintain competitive pricing structures.
Identify assortment gaps, emerging trends, and new product opportunities using store feedback and competitive analysis.

C. Purchase Planning & Inventory Management
Collaborate with supply chain teams to plan replenishment and maintain healthy stock levels.
Forecast demand and plan purchases based on historical sales, trends, and store-level insights.
Monitor ageing inventory, drive SKU rationalization, and execute exit strategies for slow-moving products.

D. Merchandising Support & Execution
Work closely with store teams to ensure effective planograms, product placement, and in-store visibility standards.
Support promotional planning through vendor-funded schemes and category-level offers.
Coordinate with catalogue and content teams to ensure accuracy in product details, pricing, and visual standards.

E. Market Intelligence & Competitive Insights
Conduct regular market and supplier visits to identify new sourcing opportunities and understand local consumer behavior.
Track category trends across home & kitchen, plastics, utilities, cleaning tools, and stationery.
Share market and competitive insights proactively to improve assortment relevance and commercial performance.

